{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires","id":1459119,"title":"Questions about Abominations ( garou vampires )","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-07T04:52:28-07:00","id":1459119,"title":"Questions about Abominations ( garou vampires )","content":"Purely theorical questions not intended to show up in a real game table. Think about a tought exercise.<br /> <br /> Since becoming an abomination - instead of simply dying - requires to botch a gnosis roll...<br /> <br /> 1) Is it possible to voluntarily botch a gnosis roll?<br /> <br /> 2) If the garou wants to become an abomination, there is any advantage or bonus or else?<br /> <br /> 3) What if the garou wears several silver items and reduces temporarily his gnosis to 0?<br /> <br /> 4) A garou heavily tainted with Wyrm has more chances to &quot;survive&quot; the Embrace?<br /> <br /> 5) Altough uncommon, garou ghouls do exist. Has they more chances to become abomination, expecially if at max Vitae capacity?<br /> <br /> 6) Could a corrupted garou make a pact with a Bane spirit to increase his chances to become an Abomination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T05:04:48-07:00","id":1459122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires#post1459119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Purely theorical questions not intended to show up in a real game table. Think about a tought exercise.<br /> <br /> Since becoming an abomination - instead of simply dying - requires to botch a gnosis roll...<br /> <br /> 1) Is it possible to voluntarily botch a gnosis roll?<br /> <br /> 2) If the garou wants to become an abomination, there is any advantage or bonus or else?<br /> <br /> 3) What if the garou wears several silver items and reduces temporarily his gnosis to 0?<br /> <br /> 4) A garou heavily tainted with Wyrm has more chances to &quot;survive&quot; the Embrace?<br /> <br /> 5) Altough uncommon, garou ghouls do exist. Has they more chances to become abomination, expecially if at max Vitae capacity?<br /> <br /> 6) Could a corrupted garou make a pact with a Bane spirit to increase his chances to become an Abomination?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No.<br /> <br /> 2) No.<br /> <br /> 3) I still think they probably die.<br /> <br /> 4) No, because vampires and the Wyrm aren't as linked as the Garou think. Even Black Spiral Dancers state that becoming an abomination is a fate worse than death because it severs you from your spiritual self.<br /> <br /> 5) I don't believe so. Garou Ghouls are much more common than abominations, though.<br /> <br /> 6) I mean, Storyteller's fiat is probably in play here. Making a deal with a Incarnae or other Totemic spirit probably is capable of overcoming the issues.<br /> <br /> I knew one guy who said, &quot;If I use the EVIL EYE from the Path of Spirit to increase the botches, can I get an Abomination?&quot;<br /> <br /> My answer being: &quot;Yes, yes you can. Which is the kind of spectacular stupidity only a Tzimisce or Tremere could come up with.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T08:22:50-07:00","id":1459138,"title":"","content":"I came up with a simpler solution for vampiric werewolves in my games. The short version of which is, they become a basic vampire, but have access to a Lycanthropy disciple that replaces one of their clan disciplines and gives them a variation of the shapeshifting part of their werewolf abilities.<br /> <br /> 1) Wolf Form: basically like the Protean power, but only a wolf and takes 3 turns (-1/BP spent) to enter or exit the form.<br /> <br /> 2) Feral Attacks: gain a claw attack akin to the Protean 2 power, its basic form costs no blood, but does only lethal damage. Spending a blood point makes it aggravated for a scene or until withdrawn.<br /> <br /> 3) Ravenous Reserves: heal aggravated damage (except from fire, sun or silver) as if it were lethal.<br /> <br /> 4) War Form: basically the same as Vicissitude 4, but no bump to brawling and you look like a Crinos.<br /> <br /> 5) Mercurial Shifting: make a Self-Control/Instinct check when entering wolf or war form (diff 5 wolf, d7 war) to reduce the turns needed or blood cost by one per success (a botch means you spend all the turns/blood but the power fails to activate.<br /> <br /> This gives you a playable vampire werewolf without needing all sort of extra drawbacks, creation mechanics that don\u2019t balance anything* and isn\u2019t hideously unbalanced relative to a vampire PC.**<br /> <br /> * if you\u2019re allowing one as a new PC it obviously pre-botched its Gnosis check; if it\u2019s created in play the PC is either dead and tries again with a new PC, or becomes OP; neither of which actually addresses the real problem that Garou and Vampire are separate game lines with different power levels needed for their specific themes and moods and so don\u2019t play well together.<br /> <br /> In point of fact, in my active Vampire campaign, werewolves are specifically built not as Garou, but as a variation of Vampires with Generation based on Rank and the clan Disciplines of Celerity, Lycanthropy and Potence (with Animalism, Auspex, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Nightmare (basically a fear-based version of Presence) and a Shamanism-based variant of Thaumaturgy are also common disciplines for them. They take no damage from sunlight, but lose all supernatural abilities during the day and only regain 1-2 \u201cblood points\u201d at sunset (depending on moon phase). Their clan weaknesses are vulnerability to silver and increased rage difficulties based on moon phase.<br /> <br /> Similarly, \u201cmages\u201d in the game aren\u2019t getting spheres, they learn specific disciplines/paths and have alternate means of gaining \u201cblood\u201d points to fuel them (so far the only types encountered by the PCs have been \u201cwitches\u201d/Verbena who recharge by ritually spilling blood and Celestial Chorus who skip disciplines entirely and just have varying levels of True Faith using one of the more flexible variations from one of the past DA editions where each rank offered the choice of a specific power... I\u2019ll develop more if they\u2019re actually needed).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve found this really helps keep the feel of a broader World of Darkness, while not overshadowing that this is a Vampire campaign (nor tempting players with greater powers than a vampire could possess... if someone wants to replace a lost PC with one, I can be more assured that it is for concept and not power gaming reasons).<br /> <br /> Anyway, that\u2019s my solution to it... abominations aren\u2019t any more powerful than other PC types; they\u2019re abominations for cultural/spiritual reasons and not because their mere existence causes mechanics to break down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T08:51:55-07:00","id":1459141,"title":"","content":"Do you mean by the RAW, or by ST fiat? I don't know about RAW, so I'll use my own takes.<br /> I tend to view vampires as kin to wraiths, and garou don't become wraiths in the first place as far as I recall, so I would actually rule that abominations aren't vampires in the first place, they're some other vitae-powered undead horror.<br /> <br /> 1) No. When Gaia decides she'd rather kill you before you stop being useful to her, you die. You don't get to say &quot;no thanks.&quot;<br /> 2) Yes, but not by much.<br /> 3) I would leave a chance of failure, but that would help too.<br /> 4) No. Even if the Triat got involved, I'd argue that despite the Beast, vampires are more static than entropic, so the Wyrm won't help you here.<br /> 5) Not sure. Did I see somewhere that these guys are allergic to vitae? In which case, I'd rule yes.<br /> 6) No","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":".  typo 09-07-2021, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T13:30:12-07:00","id":1459181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires#post1459119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Is it possible to voluntarily botch a gnosis roll?<br /> <br /> 2) If the garou wants to become an abomination, there is any advantage or bonus or else?<br /> <br /> 3) What if the garou wears several silver items and reduces temporarily his gnosis to 0?<br /> <br /> 4) A garou heavily tainted with Wyrm has more chances to &quot;survive&quot; the Embrace?<br /> <br /> 5) Altough uncommon, garou ghouls do exist. Has they more chances to become abomination, expecially if at max Vitae capacity?<br /> <br /> 6) Could a corrupted garou make a pact with a Bane spirit to increase his chances to become an Abomination?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW I mostly agree with CTP, although I would add some details.<br /> <br /> 1) No, because the cause of the roll is its nature and Gnosis, not its will;<br /> 2) No, for the same reason;<br /> 3) With so much silver the Garou is already almost dead, but the RAW is silent on it. You could make it easier, but I would make the roll without considering any silver. Per the lore, despite being a weakness silver is a sacred metal linked to Luna, and I doubt she would make it easier to Embrace a Garou;<br /> 4) No, BSDs get the exactly same roll. The problem is that the Embrace weakens your ties to the Umbra, and the Wyrm is still a spiritual entity;<br /> 5) Vitae capacity wouldn't do shit 'cause you'll drain them anyway, but I guess that the ST <i>could</i> at least consider a little benefit because the Garou is already used to Vitae, but it shouldn't be much;<br /> 6) I personally have a flexible view of &quot;story-bound&quot; methods, where it works through ST <i>fiat</i> instead of hard rules. In my personal view several spirits could do that one way or another. But this wouldn't be simple in any way. Not many spirits would be inclined to do this, no one would be cheap to convince, and the lesser the spirit, the more extra steps you would have to fulfill to give it the necessary power. Maybe it is a complex and taxing ritual, maybe it needs resources from several other spirits to be taken, maybe it is a great sacrifice and the price raises as a result.<br /> <br /> In the end that depends a lot on the chronicle and what it needs. I don't see the need for creating Abominations to be as hard as the game did, they're far less OP than the writers feared in the beginning, and the current rules already make them practically unplayable and extremely unstable as servants, so it is almost a non-issue.<br /> <br /> What really counts is the meaning it have to the lore. The Gnosis roll demonstrates that Gaia is above the Curse of Caine, and reinforces that the Garou belong to her. Changing this may be exceedingly hard or not depending on your personal view, your chronicle needs and how you explain the whatever that makes it happen, but it probably is an extremely evil act, a sin against one of the Greater Powers of Creation, and a mostly benevolent one, and condemns a spirit to be cut from its nature in a way deeper than it does to humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T20:01:14-07:00","id":1459615,"title":"","content":"Regarding #1, I'll mention that my long time Revised system interpretation (I'm not sure it fully qualifies as a house rule or not) is that any Garou who has even a single point of spendable Willpower left will automatically /instinctively use that point to get the single success on the Gnosis roll needed to avoid Botching, as essentially a final gasp of their spirit half to avoid destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T23:31:15-07:00","id":1459626,"title":"","content":"Honestly? I'd take a powerful vampire and a powerful mage working together to guarantee a garou abomination. You'd need the vampire to turn them and they'd need to be strong enough to be within kissing distance of a werewolf without turning mincemeat. You'd need the mage there to resurrect the werewolf every time the roll doesn't botch(and also probably the vampire if/when things go sideways).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T05:21:28-07:00","id":1459643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires?p=1459626#post1459626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly? I'd take a powerful vampire and a powerful mage working together to guarantee a garou abomination. You'd need the vampire to turn them and they'd need to be strong enough to be within kissing distance of a werewolf without turning mincemeat. You'd need the mage there to resurrect the werewolf every time the roll doesn't botch(and also probably the vampire if/when things go sideways).</div> </div> </div> </div>The trick would be finding a Mage with both a paradigm were such resurrection of \u201chell beasts\u201d is possible and having the spheres to pull it off.<br /> <br /> At a minimum you\u2019re looking at matter 3 (to affect/transmute a corpse), life 5 (to restore life to a complex form), spirit 4-5 (to bring the soul back to the body) and prime 2 (to reconnect the result to the flow of quintessence that keeps it alive). A separate Mind effect to backup pre-death memories may also be needed in case the death involves significant brain damage.<br /> <br /> The big one though is a paradigm that can pull off the resurrection in their paradigm and be morally inclined to repeatedly restore a creature being tortured to death to life so you can repeat the process until an undead monster is the result. We\u2019re talking straight up Nephandi to pull that off and do you really want to be beholden to a Nephandi just to get an abomination?<br /> <br /> Frankly, I\u2019d also rule that virtually no mage has sufficient understanding of the Garou\u2019s spirit and cycle of reincarnation to be able to recall the spirit once it has left. Basically you\u2019d need a high powered Dreamspeaker Barrabi before you could even start and you still have the issue that the use of Qppolithic spheres makes creation/restoration extremely difficult.<br /> <br /> A more likely approach for the Nephandi would be to just use Mind and Spirit to torture away the Garou\u2019s willpower and gnosis points and then use Entropy to inflict a curse to raise the difficulty of the Gnosis check and/or remove successes from the check. Then let the vampire (almost certainly a Baali because Nephandi are sick fucks and inflicting a blood weakness of being unable to look upon anything holy to the former Garou is exactly what they\u2019d do if they were deliberately creating an abomination).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s still a chance the Garou might still not botch, but Eggs/Omlets and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T08:42:29-07:00","id":1459657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires?p=1459643#post1459643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A more likely approach for the Nephandi would be to just use Mind and Spirit to torture away the Garou\u2019s willpower and gnosis points and then use Entropy to inflict a curse to raise the difficulty of the Gnosis check and/or remove successes from the check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use of Entropy to affect the roll is one way to do this. Depending on things, the vampire could acquire a Wonder that do this, or something similar. Torturing the Garou out of Willpower doesn't need Magick, although it could be a more humane way to do so. I'm not sure if you need to get rid of gnosis points.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that OP assumed the possibility of the Garou <i>wanting</i> to become such an immortal being, so the Garou may ease the expenditures without so much problems, and even convince/trick the others so you don't need necessarily a Nefandus or a Baali.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T09:18:25-07:00","id":1459664,"title":"","content":"In your opinion, mockery breeds like Yeren would have an easier time being Embraced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T09:56:37-07:00","id":1459666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires?p=1459664#post1459664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your opinion, mockery breeds like Yeren would have an easier time being Embraced?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends a lot on your interpretations, and can go the full range from as easy as humans to absolutely impossible.<br /> <br /> On one hand, they don't have the touch of any major spirit in their creation, and most aren't recognized by the Spirit World at all (the Yeren being an exception). On the other hand, they still have a Gnosis trait, were still created to deal with the Umbra and are still Fera by default, so they may have inherited the same blessing if this is how you interpret them.<br /> <br /> But above all, they're already an experiment, and all bets are off for how they will interact with pretty much anything. They may have an easier time, they may be just impossible due to biological instability, maybe they don't interact at all with the Embrace (especially animal-breed Mockeries), or maybe they react in really strange ways and become something stranger than Abominations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T12:09:19-07:00","id":1459676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires?p=1459657#post1459657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also keep in mind that OP assumed the possibility of the Garou <i>wanting</i> to become such an immortal being, so the Garou may ease the expenditures without so much problems, and even convince/trick the others so you don't need necessarily a Nefandus or a Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I definitely missed the willing part; probably because the general Garou sentiment on vampires and the number who stink of the Wyrm due to low Humanity make it basically akin to Garou saying \u201cI\u2019m gonna just go dance that Black Spiral and become a Wyrm-tainted monster.\u201d<br /> <br /> Basically, it would take a specific brand of nihilism plus misanthropy to make a Garou WANT to become an abomination. It\u2019s a complete abnegation of their existence, but not in a self-annihilating way because you wanna linger on after as a blood-drinking undead divorced from every natural cycle of the world.<br /> <br /> Players can certainly try to justify anything, but as a GM I would need a damnably good one before I\u2019d buy that a Garou is so disillusioned in such a specific way that they would choose to willingly become an Abomination rather than just committing suicide by Bane in hopes of a better reincarnation and assurance that you\u2019d be remembered as one who died fighting the good fight.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s impossible, but \u201cI wanna become a tortured worst of both worlds monster because they\u2019re gamebreakingly powerful in combat\u201d isn\u2019t a valid in-universe reason. The player may know the PC is just a sheet of paper they can just set aside whenever they wish, but for the PC this is \u201cknowingly damning your eternal soul\u201d territory that needs some real justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T12:37:31-07:00","id":1459677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires?p=1459676#post1459676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I definitely missed the willing part; probably because the general Garou sentiment on vampires and the number who stink of the Wyrm due to low Humanity make it basically akin to Garou saying \u201cI\u2019m gonna just go dance that Black Spiral and become a Wyrm-tainted monster.\u201d<br /> <br /> Basically, it would take a specific brand of nihilism plus misanthropy to make a Garou WANT to become an abomination. It\u2019s a complete abnegation of their existence, but not in a self-annihilating way because you wanna linger on after as a blood-drinking undead divorced from every natural cycle of the world.<br /> <br /> Players can certainly try to justify anything, but as a GM I would need a damnably good one before I\u2019d buy that a Garou is so disillusioned in such a specific way that they would choose to willingly become an Abomination rather than just committing suicide by Bane in hopes of a better reincarnation and assurance that you\u2019d be remembered as one who died fighting the good fight.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s impossible, but \u201cI wanna become a tortured worst of both worlds monster because they\u2019re gamebreakingly powerful in combat\u201d isn\u2019t a valid in-universe reason. The player may know the PC is just a sheet of paper they can just set aside whenever they wish, but for the PC this is \u201cknowingly damning your eternal soul\u201d territory that needs some real justification.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, the book where Abominations are described explicitly says that some - very rare - Garou actively try to become abominations.<br /> <br /> I quote from &quot; Under a Blood Red Moon&quot;, page 96<br /> <br /> &quot; A few Garou, fearing death, seek out vampires, offering them undying service in exchange for eternal unlife .&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Beside that, Abominations are not gamebreakingly powerful. They're much more powerful in fight than a vampire and more versatile than a Garou, but that's all.<br /> They have a much harder time learning Disciplines since next to no vampire will teach them and the can't learn new Gifts except those Bane-related.<br /> They must spend willpower just to be able to function properly due their cronic depression.<br /> They lose their regeneration and must rely on vitae healing, which is by far less effective.<br /> They share the weakness of vampires about fire and sunlight. Even if not exposed to light, they're crippled during dayhours.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, the only valid reason to become an Abomination is immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 09-11-2021, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T14:38:30-07:00","id":1459695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires?p=1459676#post1459676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s impossible, but \u201cI wanna become a tortured worst of both worlds monster because they\u2019re gamebreakingly powerful in combat\u201d isn\u2019t a valid in-universe reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. But &quot;I'm afraid of death&quot; is.<br /> <br /> Garou aren't all equal and not all of them are exemplars of their culture. How many people IRL live in cultures that talk about reincarnation, heaven, honor or so many other reasons to not be afraid of death, or at least of a &quot;good death&quot;, and yet those people are pretty much afraid of dying.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of reading the lore so strictly as to forbid player characters from wanting different things, and definitely don't think Abominations are as strong as some people think. &quot;Moralizing&quot; the game in lieu of letting people having fun with it is one of the most abject long standing traditions of WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T15:27:52-07:00","id":1459699,"title":"","content":"As near as I can tell, aside from all the intangible drawbacks an Abomination loses access to so much of a normal werewolf's mechanical advantages that one would be just as well off making a regular vampire who knows Horrid Form and customizing it to <i>look</i> like a war-form werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T15:51:31-07:00","id":1459702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires?p=1459699#post1459699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As near as I can tell, aside from all the intangible drawbacks an Abomination loses access to so much of a normal werewolf's mechanical advantages that one would be just as well off making a regular vampire who knows Horrid Form and customizing it to <i>look</i> like a war-form werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few other tangible benefits, but they're not much to brag about.<br /> <br /> IIRC you keep actually more powers than you lose. Namely you keep any Gift you already know, the ability to step sideways and your Gnosis and Rage traits. But your Gnosis is harder to fill and is so threatened by your new Path that you should think twice before making... anything, really. The Umbra is more dangerous and even Banes are loath to teach you new Gifts without a hearty dose of extra convincing, even because they know they can ask more from your sorry ass.<br /> <br /> Rage I'm not sure if it changes in the slightest, but Frenzy is probably more likely to happen if you don't take care.<br /> <br /> Your gifts are your gifts. You probably paid for them anyway, so keeping them is more &quot;not loosing even further&quot; than actually gaining something, and I would rule that an Abomination do not get 3 free Discipline dots. Those dots represent the neonate having some training before the start of the game, so the Abomination would have to buy them apiece. Not that it changes much, it got 3 level 1 Gifts for free, but most level 1 Gifts are quite lackluster.<br /> <br /> But yeah, to be honest a Garou Ghoul is far more OP than an Abomination by far. So the mechanical benefit to the Abomination is... immortality without Blood Bond and that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T12:58:07-07:00","id":1459957,"title":"","content":"I too thought about the silver thing.<br /> I think the biggest issue is that, if it was something you could reliably do, a lot of vampires would do it. I mean... well there's the issue of finding a werewolf, avoiding reprisals, and elders not trying to kill the thing out of a fear that it has a greater potential than normal kindred, but inevitably it'd become a <i>thing</i> and the setting would become far more messy.<br /> <br /> The other big issue is that, well, really like the idea that vampires can do anything provided they've got the XP, and there's a big issue with abominations because they have abilities you simply can't get with XP as a vampire. Gifts and stepping sideways can likely be reinterpreted as demonic investments, but garou shapeshifting is something you can only crudely approximate with elder level disciplines.<br /> <br /> Maegar are better. Really. <br /> <br /> Perhaps I'd fix Abominations by having their abilities melt down into xp or a learnable discipline or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T16:28:35-07:00","id":1459976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1459119-questions-about-abominations-garou-vampires?p=1459957#post1459957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other big issue is that, well, really like the idea that vampires can do anything provided they've got the XP, and there's a big issue with abominations because they have abilities you simply can't get with XP as a vampire. Gifts and stepping sideways can likely be reinterpreted as demonic investments, but garou shapeshifting is something you can only crudely approximate with elder level disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much. Horrid Form gets pretty close, and it is level 4. And Auspex 5 arguably launches you in the Umbra, just not named so because Vampires don't interact with the realm frequently enough in their own game. Arguably, but in a game where I intended this level of crossover for any reason I would rule so anyways, so everyone have a chance to play in the same playground.<br /> <br /> It also depends to with whom you compares the character. An Abomination is certainly a strong Vampire character with Shapechange, Stepping Sideways and Rage before Disciplines kick in. Not invincible, despite what some people believe, but strong. But it isn't really stronger than a Werewolf. Talking only mechanic benefits it is a trade-off of Healing for access to Disciplines, good-ish, not excellent.<br /> <br /> On both cases the difficulty on making it happen and the rules on Gnosis, Humanity and Harano for the Abomination are more than enough to make it rare even if no roll to stop it existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}